{"id":"e03t2","name":"Patient Portal Sessions","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","events_df","gap_minutes"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Patients use an online portal to book appointments and read their results. The product team wants to understand how patients use it, session by session.</p>\n<p>You are given <code>events_df</code> with the columns <code>patient_id</code> (string), <code>ts</code> (timestamp) and <code>page</code> (string), and an integer <code>gap_minutes</code>. Rows are not sorted, and a patient can have several events at the same timestamp.</p>\n<p>For each patient, events are grouped into <b>sessions</b>: in time order, an event starts a new session when it comes <b>strictly more</b> than <code>gap_minutes</code> minutes after the previous event of the same patient. The first event of a patient always starts a session.</p>\n<p>The <b>duration</b> of a session is the time between its first and its last event, in minutes (a session with one event lasts <code>0</code> minutes). A session is <b>converted</b> if one of its events has the page <code>\"booking_confirmed\"</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per patient with:</p>\n<ol><li><code>patient_id</code>;</li><li><code>sessions</code> - the number of sessions;</li><li><code>avg_minutes</code> - the average duration of the sessions, rounded to 1 decimal;</li><li><code>max_minutes</code> - the longest duration, rounded to 1 decimal;</li><li><code>converted</code> - the number of converted sessions.</li></ol>\n<p>Sort by <code>patient_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>events_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>patient_id</th><th>ts</th><th>page</th></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td><td>home</td></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:10:00</td><td>booking_confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:45:00</td><td>results</td></tr><tr><td>p2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td><td>home</td></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:55:30</td><td>home</td></tr><tr><td>p2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:30:00</td><td>search</td></tr></table></div><p><code>gap_minutes = 30</code></p><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>patient_id</th><th>sessions</th><th>avg_minutes</th><th>max_minutes</th><th>converted</th></tr><tr><td>p1</td><td>2</td><td>10.3</td><td>10.5</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>p2</td><td>1</td><td>30.0</td><td>30.0</td><td>0</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>For <code>p1</code>, the event at <code>10:45</code> comes 35 minutes after <code>10:10</code>, so it starts a second session.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, events_df: DataFrame, gap_minutes: int) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return events_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["sessions","lag","somme cumulée","Window","groupBy / agg"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"events_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"patient_id STRING, ts TIMESTAMP, page STRING","rows":[["p1","2026-03-01 10:00:00","home"],["p1","2026-03-01 10:10:00","booking_confirmed"],["p1","2026-03-01 10:45:00","results"],["p2","2026-03-01 09:00:00","home"],["p1","2026-03-01 10:55:30","home"],["p2","2026-03-01 09:30:00","search"]]}},"gap_minutes":30},"expected":{"columns":["patient_id","sessions","avg_minutes","max_minutes","converted"],"rows":[["p1",2,10.3,10.5,1],["p2",1,30.0,30.0,0]]}},{"input":{"events_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"patient_id STRING, ts TIMESTAMP, page STRING","rows":[["z","2026-03-02 08:00:00","booking_confirmed"],["z","2026-03-02 08:00:00","booking_confirmed"],["z","2026-03-02 08:05:00","home"]]}},"gap_minutes":5},"expected":{"columns":["patient_id","sessions","avg_minutes","max_minutes","converted"],"rows":[["z",1,5.0,5.0,1]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}